    },
    "body": "Measured from verdicts-29m.tsv on main by splitting the 189 failures by terminal punctuation. CORRECTION: 64 completed-but-rejected, not 62 — earlier comments in this line said 62 and the per-row table gives 64 rows with no_terminal=0. THE SEPARATOR IS LENGTH, NOT FORM: median reply_words 10 completed against 31 cut, and repeat5 5% against 34%, so repetition was a symptom of running long rather than a mechanism of the real failures. THE WELL-POSED-ROW EFFECT WAS ENTIRELY THE CAP, confirmed at the failure level: completed failures sit 21/21/22 across tiers. THEY ARE REJECTED ON BOTH AXES: 64% neither fluent nor relevant, every form marker low — bad answers, not mis-formatted ones. And they are diffuse (41/20/3), firing the pre-registered stop condition, so no intervention is proposed or run. CONSEQUENCE: criterion 1's reply-panel half cannot carry the criterion — diffuse failures, a cap that is not the constraint, a judge-borne instrument with no frozen checks, and a macOS-only baseline until Run A re-grounded it. Recommendation recorded: deterministic checks in the v4/v5 style, and a diagnosable target. CPU only, no pod, no generation, no grading.",
